,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.10609298305571307,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.05719658246881676,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":28.5,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.03441498796865128,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":26.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.03555048374387426,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":42.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10972710723337725,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.02988859344235051,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":87.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03616,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":24.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Westamerica Bancorporation operates as a bank holding company for Westamerica Bank that provides various banking products and services to individual and commercial customers in the United States. The company accepts various deposit products from local businesses and professionals, as well as retail savings and checking accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. Its loan portfolio includes commercial, commercial real estate, residential real estate, real estate construction, consumer installment loans, as well as indirect automobile loans. The company serves small businesses, professionals, and consumers. The company was formerly known as Independent Bankshares Corporation and changed its name to Westamerica Bancorporation in 1983. Westamerica Bancorporation was founded in 1884 and is headquartered in San Rafael, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David L. Payne | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $802,645 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 608 people. Revenue per employee of $424K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $197K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Westamerica Bancorporation is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.4B market cap on $258M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 46 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 11.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 32% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Grupo Financiero Galicia (NASDAQ:GGAL) and Westamerica Bancorporation (NASDAQ:WABC) Head-To-Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/grupo-financiero-galicia-nasdaqggal-and-westamer